**Overall verdict: CORRECT WITH FIXES.** The multiplier \(w\) and the change \(M=N^\mu\) introduce no obstruction to LV6 or batch smoothness. The “Consequence” follows from the listed internal results after correcting the coefficient index, updating the irreducibility bookkeeping, and making the reducible-field branch explicit. I left the repository unchanged.

The table in [ldbound §6.1](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/ldbound_results.md:497) covers most dependencies, although its single row grouping C/H/E/X/SQ/Wiedemann hides several checks.

| Item and location in LV6 | Verdict | Transfer check |
|---|---|---|
| [Setting, \(\psi\), norm identities and row equation](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/lv6_results.md:84) | **CORRECT** | The map requires \(N\mid F(g_0,g_1)\), which \(Nw\) supplies. Neither the norm identity nor equation (1.1) requires equality to \(N\). Replace the field tuple by \((g_0,g_1,w,c)\). |
| [Prop LV6’s field hypotheses](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/lv6_results.md:114) | **CORRECT** | Its proof is pointwise for every accepted field. Primitivity, irreducibility, and the required units modulo \(N\) must still be checked. No distributional theorem about the selected fields is needed here. |
| [Degree drop and leading-coefficient gcd](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/lv6_results.md:455) | **CORRECT** | After \((g_1,N)=1\), \(f_d\equiv Nwg_0^{-d}\not\equiv0\pmod {g_1}\), since \(w>g_1\). Also \(0<|f_d|<N\), so a nonunit leading coefficient produces a proper factor. |
